 "poem": "14",
 "name": "the black with no walls",
 "look": "all black, no room, no floor; one faint noise-bent open horizon of light that never closes; later a faint ring of floor for the dance and the old door standing alone",
 "light": "base black breathing between two levels; the horizon a thin pale band; the only warm light the door",
